.TH REMOVE_STALE_TEMPLATES 1 "2026-08-26" "rptsched-cleanup" "rptsched-cleanup Manual"
.SH NAME
remove_stale_templates.py \- quarantine stale manual saved templates and prune their schedlist lines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remove_stale_templates.py
.B \-\-data\-dir
.I DIR
.B \-\-quarantine\-dir
.I DIR
.B \-\-logs\-report\-dir
.I DIR
.B \-\-logs\-hist\-dir
.I DIR
[\fB\-\-index\-cache\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-years\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-exclude\-owner\fR \fIOWNER\fR ...]
[\fB\-\-exclude\-owner\-regex\fR \fIPATTERN\fR ...]
[\fB\-\-execute\fR | \fB\-\-restore\fR \fIRUN_DIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B remove_stale_templates.py
finds
.I "stale saved templates"
in a Symphony ILS report\-scheduler data directory (\fIrptsched\fR) and
moves their files into quarantine, removing the corresponding line from
.IR schedlist .

Candidate selection does
.B not
use \fIschedlist\fR's own \fBlast_run\fR/\fBcreated\fR fields as an
activity signal \- empirical testing found those fields never update for
the most common real usage pattern (ad hoc "Run Now" on a manual
template), which caused a real production incident. Instead, activity is
looked up in two independent log sources outside \fIrptsched\fR:
\fILogs/Report/\fR (unconditional \fB"Finished report"\fR lines, no
owner) and \fILogs/Hist/\fR (owner\-attributed, decoded via Symphony's
own \fBlogprint\fR | \fBtranslate\fR pipeline, and the only source that
sees ad hoc runs at all). See
\fI2026\-08\-31\-remove\-stale\-templates\-log\-based\-redesign.md\fR for
the full design and empirical basis.

A saved template (one row of \fIschedlist\fR, plus its \fI<id>.set\fR /
\fI<id>.selans\fR file group) is a stale\-template candidate when
.B all
of the following hold:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B frequency_flag
is \fBn\fR \- the template is manual (run by hand only), not on a
recurring Symphony schedule.
.IP \(bu 2
.B owner
is not excluded by any \fB\-\-exclude\-owner\fR or
\fB\-\-exclude\-owner\-regex\fR entry passed on the command line.
.IP \(bu 2
Its \fB(report_source, description)\fR pair shows no activity in
\fILogs/Report/\fR within \fB\-\-years\fR, \fBand\fR its \fB(report_source,
description, owner)\fR triple shows no activity in \fILogs/Hist/\fR
within \fB\-\-years\fR either. A match in \fIeither\fR source protects
the template \- this is deliberate defense in depth given the category's
history.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcreated\fR is at least \fB\-\-years\fR years before today \- a
template that's simply new is protected even with no log activity yet,
since \fBcreated\fR (unlike \fBlast_run\fR) stays a trustworthy one\-time
stamp for manual templates specifically.
.RE
.PP
Unlike orphans, every stale\-template candidate has a live \fIschedlist\fR
line. This tool removes that line \- via write\-temp\-file plus atomic
rename, never an in\-place edit \- so nothing is left dangling. Restoring
a run re\-inserts the exact removed lines back into the \fIcurrent\fR
schedlist.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-data\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to the \fIrptsched\fR data directory to scan and modify. Required in
every mode, including \fB\-\-restore\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-quarantine\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to the quarantine directory that holds run subfolders. Created if it
does not already exist. Required in every mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-logs\-report\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to Symphony's \fILogs/Report/\fR directory. Required for dry\-run
and \fB\-\-execute\fR; not needed for \fB\-\-restore\fR, which replays a
past run's exact removed lines rather than re\-evaluating activity.
.TP
.BR \-\-logs\-hist\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to Symphony's \fILogs/Hist/\fR directory. Same required\-ness as
\fB\-\-logs\-report\-dir\fR. Decoding this source shells out to
\fBlogprint\fR and \fBtranslate\fR, which only exist on the production
server.
.TP
.BR \-\-index\-cache\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Where to persist the activity\-index cache between runs, so unchanged
\fILogs/Hist/\fR months (the expensive source to decode) aren't
reprocessed every invocation. Defaults to a file under
\fB\-\-quarantine\-dir\fR. Only used by \fB\-\-execute\fR \- dry\-run
never writes anything, including this cache.
.TP
.BR \-\-years " " \fIN\fR
Inactivity threshold in years, applied to both the log\-activity lookup
and, as a floor protecting new templates, \fBcreated\fR. Default: \fB3\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-owner " " \fIOWNER\fR
Exclude templates whose \fBowner\fR is an exact, case\-insensitive match
for \fIOWNER\fR. Repeatable \- pass once per owner to exclude a specific
set. No substring matching: \fB\-\-exclude\-owner ACQ1\fR excludes only an
owner literally named \fBACQ1\fR, not \fBACQ10\fR. Not set by default \-
this script excludes no owners unless told to.
.TP
.BR \-\-exclude\-owner\-regex " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude templates whose \fBowner\fR matches regex \fIPATTERN\fR via
case\-insensitive, unanchored \fBre.search\fR. Repeatable. Breadth is the
caller's responsibility through regex syntax \- e.g. \fBACQ\fR matches
\fBACQ1\fR, \fBACQHQ\fR, and \fBjsmith\-acq\fR anywhere in the owner
string; \fB^ACQ\fR matches only owners starting with it. Not set by
default.
.TP
.B \-\-execute
Perform the move and the \fIschedlist\fR rewrite. Without this flag the
script runs in dry\-run mode and writes nothing.
.TP
.BR \-\-restore " " \fIRUN_DIR\fR
Reverse a previous \fB\-\-execute\fR run: restore quarantined files, then
re\-insert their removed \fIschedlist\fR lines. Mutually exclusive with
\fB\-\-execute\fR.
.SH MODES
.SS Dry run (default)
Prints the count of stale\-template candidates, the total count of manual
templates in \fIschedlist\fR (regardless of staleness or owner exclusion),
and total files, then one line per candidate: id, description,
report_source, owner, frequency_flag, created, and its file list.
\fBlast_run\fR is deliberately not shown \- it plays no part in the
decision and displaying it invites the exact misreading that caused the
original production incident. Nothing on disk is touched, including the
activity\-index cache.
.SS Execute
With \fB\-\-execute\fR, the script:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Finds candidates as described above. If none are found, prints a message
and exits 0 without creating a run subfolder.
.IP 2. 4
Creates \fB\-\-quarantine\-dir\fR/templates_\fITIMESTAMP\fR and moves each
candidate's file group into it, writing \fImanifest.csv\fR (same
mechanics and partial\-failure behavior as \fBremove_orphans.py\fR(1)).
.IP 3. 4
Writes the exact removed \fIschedlist\fR lines, verbatim and in id order,
to \fIremoved_schedlist_lines.txt\fR in the run subfolder.
.IP 4. 4
Rewrites \fIschedlist\fR to drop those lines, via a temp file plus atomic
rename.
.RE
.IP
Steps 3 and 4 only run after every file in step 2 has been moved
successfully; a move failure aborts before \fIschedlist\fR is touched,
so a failed run never produces a dangling \fIschedlist\fR line.
.SS Restore
With \fB\-\-restore\fR \fIRUN_DIR\fR, the script:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Restores quarantined files exactly as \fBremove_orphans.py\fR(1)'s
\fB\-\-restore\fR does: idempotent, resumable, skips rows whose
\fIdest_path\fR no longer exists, aborts on a \fIsource_path\fR
collision.
.IP 2. 4
Reads \fIRUN_DIR\fR/removed_schedlist_lines.txt (if present \- an empty
result is treated as "no lines to reinsert", not an error) and re\-inserts
each line into the \fBcurrent\fR schedlist at the position matching its
\fBcreated\fR timestamp, without disturbing the relative order of any
line that wasn't touched. \fIschedlist\fR's real on\-disk order is
chronological by \fBcreated\fR, not alphabetical by id.
.RE
.IP
The re\-insert step is idempotent independently of the file\-restore step:
it skips any line whose id is already present in the current schedlist,
so it is safe even if the current schedlist has legitimate edits made
after the original removal run, and safe to re\-run.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \- including a clean dry run, an execute run that found zero
candidates, or a restore that skipped everything because it was already
complete.
.TP
.B 1
A move, schedlist rewrite, or restore operation failed; or
\fB\-\-logs\-report\-dir\fR/\fB\-\-logs\-hist\-dir\fR contains zero files
within \fB\-\-years\fR (refused rather than silently treating every
manual template as inactive \- likely a wrong or unmounted path).
Details are printed to stderr.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <data\-dir>/schedlist
Read to find candidates; rewritten in place (atomically) by
\fB\-\-execute\fR to drop matched lines, and again by \fB\-\-restore\fR to
re\-insert them.
.TP
.I <quarantine\-dir>/templates_<timestamp>/manifest.csv
File\-move record, same format as \fBremove_orphans.py\fR(1).
.TP
.I <quarantine\-dir>/templates_<timestamp>/removed_schedlist_lines.txt
The exact \fIschedlist\fR lines removed by this run, one per line,
verbatim. Never deleted \- required for \fB\-\-restore\fR and doubles as
an audit record.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview stale templates using the default 3\-year threshold:
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-logs\-report\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Report \-\-logs\-hist\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Hist
.TP
Use a 5\-year threshold instead:
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-logs\-report\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Report \-\-logs\-hist\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Hist \-\-years 5
.TP
Execute a run:
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-logs\-report\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Report \-\-logs\-hist\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Hist \-\-execute
.TP
Exclude a specific list of owners:
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-logs\-report\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Report \-\-logs\-hist\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Hist \-\-exclude\-owner ACQ1 \-\-exclude\-owner ACQ2
.TP
Exclude any owner containing "ACQ", regardless of case:
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-logs\-report\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Report \-\-logs\-hist\-dir /software/WYLD/Unicorn/Logs/Hist \-\-exclude\-owner\-regex ACQ
.TP
Undo a specific run (files and schedlist lines both, no log dirs needed):
.B remove_stale_templates.py \-\-data\-dir ./rptsched \-\-quarantine\-dir ./quarantine \-\-restore ./quarantine/templates_20260826_140501
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR remove_orphans.py (1),
.BR sync_operator_field.py (1)

Domain reference: \fIrptsched\-domain\-reference.md\fR in the
rptsched\-cleanup repository \- see "Inactivity rule" and "Owner
exclusion" under "Definitions", and the \fIschedlist\fR field table.
.SH CAVEATS
Requires Python 3.6.8, standard library only.

The \fB\-\-years\fR value must match between the run that removed a
template and any later reasoning about it; restore replays the exact
removed line rather than re\-evaluating staleness, so it is unaffected by
a later change to \fB\-\-years\fR.

This tool only ever considers manual templates (\fBfrequency_flag ==
"n"\fR). Recurring\-schedule templates are the separate, not\-yet\-built
"scheduled report removal candidates" category described in the
project's CLAUDE.md.
